WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:04.715
Today we will look at the matrix method for
solving

2
00:00:04.715 --> 00:00:07.770
systems of linear equations. This method

3
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:11.779
is convenient for systems of low order and is
based

4
00:00:11.779 --> 00:00:15.160
on the properties of matrix multiplication.

5
00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.833
If the number of equations in the system
equals the number

6
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:23.620
of unknowns and the determinant of the matrix

7
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:28.610
is not zero, the matrix method is used.

8
00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:35.500
In matrix form, we write the system like this:
here A is the coefficient matrix

9
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:41.960
of the system, B is the matrix of constant
terms, and X is the column matrix

10
00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.570
of the unknowns. The solution of the system
has the following form.

11
00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:51.647
Let us solve a system of linear equations by
the

12
00:00:51.647 --> 00:00:54.480
matrix method. We compute the determinant

13
00:00:54.480 --> 00:01:01.880
of the coefficient matrix. Since Δ is not
zero, the system has a unique solution.

14
00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:10.060
We solve the system of linear equations by the
matrix method. To continue,

15
00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:13.500
we form the matrices A, B and X.

16
00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:21.920
We find the inverse matrix A⁻¹. We compute the
determinant of A,

17
00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:28.350
using cofactor expansion along the first row.
Now we find the

18
00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:30.310
cofactors.

19
00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:38.650
Using the cofactors we have found, we build
the inverse matrix.

20
00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:44.885
Now the matrix X: we find the product of the

21
00:01:44.885 --> 00:01:49.180
inverse matrix and matrix B. As a result

22
00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.840
we get the solution matrix of the system of
equations.

23
00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:59.850
To sum up: the matrix method is convenient for
solving systems of linear equations

24
00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:06.790
in which the number of equations matches the
number of unknowns and the determinant

25
00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:13.550
of the coefficient matrix is nonzero. If the
system has more than three equations,

26
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:19.090
finding the inverse matrix requires laborious
calculations.
